  "title": "Course Description",
  "body": " Course Description  MATH 221 Calculus III  A study of conic sections, vectors in two and three dimensions, dot and cross products and their applications to geometry, equations of lines and planes, quadratic surfaces, polar, cylindrical, and spherical coordinates, and functions of several variables, partial derivatives, differentials, directional derivatives, gradients, optimization problems, multiple integrals and their applications.  Prerequisite: MATH 220 Calculus II with a minimum grade of C (2.00) or higher.  "
